# kdc calibration: Kindle PaperWhite 4 (ED060KC4 panel, fw 5.18.1.1.1)
# 2026-11-07, kdc-cal at 18-19 C, 1-frame pulses (kdc-pulse.sh install 1).
install 1

# Response curves (state model, used when present). Levels 0=K .. 3=W,
# n = pulses:  dark(n) = 3 exp(-(n/TAU)^P)  from white,
#              light(n) = 3 (1 - exp(-(n/TAU)^P))  from black.
# Fitted to stage-1 ladder photos (rms 0.09 / 0.10 levels); predicts the
# stage-2 ladders (from D and L) within ~0.2-0.3 levels.
dark   11.1 1.02
light   6.3 1.24

# Per-level pulse steps (preferred over the curves above when present):
# levels moved by one pulse at levels 0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3. Fitted jointly
# to all six ladders (W>, K>, D>W, D>K, L>W, L>K): rms 0.137 levels.
# Darkening is weak near black with 1-frame pulses (0.02 level/pulse at 0.5).
dark_steps  0.000 0.018 0.096 0.161 0.295 0.245 0.163
light_steps 0.228 0.350 0.377 0.350 0.298 0.050 0.000

# Dose matrix (dose-counting fallback). Pulses per transition.
# Rows: from K D L W. Columns: to K D L W. Darkening is ~3x slower than
# lightening with short pulses.
#    K   D   L   W
K    0   3   6  10
D   20   0   3   9
L   22   4   0   8
W   30  11   5   0
